.DS_store

# All build output lives here: the compiler's own objects + generated parser/lexer + binary, under
# out/<os>-<arch>/ so a host and a container build coexist — and anything `kama build` emits, which
# is the same `out/` a seeded project gets (docs/targets.md). One rule covers both.
#
# ⚠️ This file used to carry ~30 more lines: a blanket `*.c` / `*.wasm` / `*.html` / `*.js`, a
# `tests/*` allowlist INVERSION with four `!` rescues, and six more `!` rescues scattered below to
# un-ignore real sources those blankets swallowed. None of it was ever an ignore policy — it was
# scaffolding around a compiler that wrote generated files next to their sources. It doesn't any
# more (`genDir` follows `-o`, and run_tests.sh builds every fixture under a mktemp dir), so the
# scaffolding is gone. `tools/check-clean-tree.sh` is what keeps it gone: it fails if a build leaves
# anything behind, which is a real check, unlike an ignore rule that hides the evidence.
#
# So: DON'T re-add a blanket pattern here when you see a stray artifact. Find what wrote it.
out/

# throwaway language probes and disposable local output — benchmark logs, a scratch httpd binary.
# A probe worth keeping becomes a tests/ fixture.
.scratch/

# the root compiler binary (anchored to root so it doesn't also ignore bench/src/kama/)
/kama

# per-machine local manifest override (deep-merges over kama.json; dev-local, never committed — see M5)
kama.local.json
**/kama.local.json

# fetched native SDKs (wgpu-native for native --webgpu) — never vendored; tools/fetch-webgpu.sh fills it
third_party/

# benchmark build artifacts (the bench corpus has its own output root, not the compiler's out/)
bench/build/

# dotnet build output (lands in the bind-mounted bench source dir)
bench/src/csharp/bin/
bench/src/csharp/obj/

# qemu core dumps (from emulated-arch crashes)
*.core

# local secrets — seed from .env.example
.env

# assembled site output (from tools/build-site) and packaged extension
/_site/
*.vsix

# the site generator's dependency (regenerated by `npm ci`; the lockfile is tracked)
/node_modules/

# VS Code extension dependencies (regenerated by `npm install`; the lockfile is tracked)
editor/vscode/node_modules/

# tree-sitter CLI (a 20 MB prebuilt binary fetched by the package's install script;
# the lockfile is tracked and PINS the version tools/check-treesitter.sh regenerates with)
tree-sitter-kama/node_modules/

# the Zed extension's Rust build output (Zed compiles this itself; Cargo.lock is tracked)
editor/zed/target/
